MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_001: Ah, if it isn't Ursula. Heading out to enjoy a bit of\nsketching in nature?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_002: I am. Though I don't recall telling you about\nmy hobbies.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_003: The wind knows all, my dear. I must tell you I've\nbeen known to dabble in the visual arts myself.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_004: I've thought for a while now that you and I might\ndeepen our friendship over a few drawing sessions.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_005: Spinning lies to build common ground is an old trick\nand will get you nowhere.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_006: Lies? That's a bit harsh. I'm telling you it's all true.\nHere, allow me to show you the proof.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_007: A notebook? What is this? *gasp*
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_008: Hmhm. Men and gods alike have been struck\nspeechless upon seeing such sublime artistry.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_009: Go on. I look forward to your honest opinion.\nIt's well drawn, is it not?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_010: Y-you drew this? What is this? A monster crawling\nwith maggots?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_011: "Monster"? What do you mean? I have captured with\nmere pencil and paper the beauty within you.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_012: Ah! This is meant to represent ME?!
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_013: I can't see the connection. This is...obscene! I'd have\nan easier time believing this is a drawing of vomit.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_014: Hmmm. That is a...creative...take on a work of\nsublime beauty.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_015: Still, you might try critiquing artistic endeavors\nfrom a more refined perspective.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_016: Are you questioning my sense of aesthetics?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_017: Come now, there's no need for such a dour look.\nI simply have confidence in my artistic abilities.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_018: I have drawn for Kalla, goddess of the arts, many\ntimes and have never heard a whit of criticism.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_019: Never? Looking at it objectively, I can only see\nit as an affront.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_020: I have an idea... We'll show your drawing and mine\nto my lady Kalla...
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_021: And we'll ask her to critique them both. Fair enough?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_022: I will arrange the details with my goddess—all you\nhave to do is supply your drawing.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_C_023: I accept your proposal, but...does Kalla have time for\nsuch trivial matters?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_001: How can this be?! Ahhh... I am done. Done!
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_002: You look like you've seen a ghost, Sirocco.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_003: Ursula...you were right. So very right. Go on, laugh\nat me. For I am pitiful after all.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_004: What are you talking about?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_005: I told you that I would show our drawings to my\nbeloved goddess Kalla. Don't you remember?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_006: Well, I received her critiques just the other day.\nYour landscape... It earned high praise. Very high.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_007: Meanwhile, the portrait drawn by my own hand...\nIt was received more poorly than a blustering storm.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_008: Well, to be frank, it wasn't clear you'd intended\nto depict a human being.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_009: But you said you'd shown your art to Kalla before,\ndidn't you?
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_010: You were proud of the fact she'd never returned\na single word of criticism, as I recall.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_011: Yes, she explained that. And I quote, "Your drawings\nwere so horrible they rendered me speechless."
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_012: Thinking back on it now, I realize that she never\nsaid a word...not of criticism, nor of praise!
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_013: Ah...
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_014: Now I know why my lady gave me such avid counsel\nabout my poems but shut her lips about my sketches.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_015: I should have known what that meant. But I was so\nsure my artwork's beauty had struck her speechless.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_016: So that's what you meant about striking men and\ngods speechless with sublime artistry...
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_017: Exactly! I spoke with conviction born from my\nlived experience, and yet...
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_018: Pft... Snrk... Hahaha! Oh, this is too much!
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_019: A-ah...
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_020: All this time...you had no idea what it was that\nstunned her into silence! Ahaha!
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_021: I'm sorry... I couldn't help myself.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_022: I did not expect you to laugh at me... No, I was sure\nyou'd freeze me out with a storm of ice.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_023: Instead I got to see a warm smile blow across that\nstrict business face of yours. I shall call that a win.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_024: You don't give up, do you? I admire your spirit.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_025: Ah, you've taken a liking to me, then. May I suggest\nthat tonight, you and I—
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_026: If you're hoping for a tryst, I must decline. That said,\nlet me see...
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_027: I could give you some drawing tips. I feel I owe you,\nas an apology for laughing.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_028: Then, if you improve, you may even get praise\nfrom Kalla.
MID_SE_Urs_Sci_B_029: A perfect idea, Ursula! Anything to improve my\nbeloved goddess's opinion of my art!